 "kind": "recipe",
 "metadata": {
  "alignment": "unspecified",
  "description": "GLM-5.3-Flash on two DGX Sparks with the TensorFold engine (exact decoding, custom CUDA kernels JIT-compiled on first start), one rank per Spark over the ConnectX-7 link with RoCE all-gathers. Serves MiaAI-Lab's EXL3 TR3 4 bpw checkpoint with a 1,048,576-token window, up to 4 concurrent requests sharing an FP8 KV pool, DFlash2 and copy drafts, 4-bit dense weights, image and video input, tool calling and structured outputs. Based on MiaAI-Lab's two-Spark TensorFold kit (ed026ef9, Apache-2.0) on TensorFold v0.5.0 (MIT) with her 52 patches; a different engine from the vLLM two-Spark recipe. Upstream claims 60.4 tok/s for one request and 108.8 tok/s aggregate at 4, about 1,950 tok/s prefill and GSM8K 98.0 percent / HumanEval 97.6 percent, all unmeasured here. Licences, for information: the checkpoint is under the ShapleyMcG License 1.0 (attribution required); the DFlash2 drafter is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 (non-commercial) and is not used with the MTP drafter option.",
  "tags": [
   "dflash2",
   "engine",
   "exl3",
   "glm-5.3",
   "image-input",
   "kernel-jit",
   "multimodal",
   "reasoning",
   "roce",
   "spark",
   "structured-outputs",
   "tensorfold",
   "tool-use",
   "video-input"
  ],
  "title": "GLM 5.3 Flash EXL3 DFlash2 TensorFold two Sparks"
 },
